 "description": "One request. The forwarded body holds 4,000 text bytes, an image of 2,000,000 bytes (8,000 tokens at the fixed price) and a thinking block counted at 1,000 tokens. The provider bills 2,350 tokens, below the media price, so check 11 fails: the library cuts the media to the bill less the least the text can cost (4,000 x 0.05 = 200 tokens). No room is left for the count, so the counts are dropped, and the signature's fixed price is cut to 0. The cause is the media, so media_tokens is reported and opaque_tokens is not. The operator cuts m0 by 2,000 bytes: 2,000 x 0.05 = 100 tokens saved, the lowest the bill allows.",
